  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "At the San Cha Mountain inheritance grounds the text calls him “one who had dyed the sky blue before.” He kills three Shang clan elders with poison and lifts demonic path morale until Wu clan’s rank four Elder Wu Tong Shen holds him back two days later and restores equilibrium.",
      "chapters": [
        326
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_san_cha_mountain",
        "fac_shang_clan",
        "fac_wu_clan",
        "char_wu_tong_shen"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He has long black hair, pale-green skin, and green pupils that faintly flash as if cold fires burn in them.",
      "chapters": [
        345
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He is a thin Gu Master in a dark blue robe, with a gloomy gaze.",
      "chapters": [
        387
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Narration places him among the four rank four peak stage Gu Masters on the mountain who can kill Fang Yuan.",
      "chapters": [
        344
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rank-four-peak-contest",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_masters",
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When the three kings inheritance opens, he charges from the east as a poison path Gu Master with long black hair, pale-green skin, and green pupils. He stands with Kong Ri Tian, Wu Shen Tong, and Yi Chong as the mountain’s strongest present Gu Masters, sometimes collaborates with Kong Ri Tian when pressed, and chooses King Xin’s inheritance after the stalemate. Other Gu Masters who fell into his trap in King Xin Inheritance last time warn each other to avoid him this time.",
      "chapters": [
        345
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rank-four-peak-contest",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_master",
        "char_kong_ri_tian",
        "char_wu_shen_tong",
        "char_yi_chong",
        "inh_king_xin_inheritance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In Fang Yuan’s previous-life memories, Yi Huo defeats him and Kong Ri Tian and rules for a time until Long Qing Tian, driven anxious by that dominance, poisons Yi Huo with blue halo Gu and forces Yi Huo back to Shang Clan City for Doctor Su Shou’s treatment.",
      "chapters": [
        355
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rivalry-with-yi-huo",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_yi_huo",
        "gu_blue_halo_gu",
        "loc_shang_clan_city",
        "char_doctor_su_shou"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "At a later opening, the text names him “He who once dyed the sky blue,” rank four peak stage. He attacks Yi Huo with a greenish-blue poison palm, then enters King Xin Inheritance with Kong Ri Tian after Yi Huo suppresses the field.",
      "chapters": [
        356
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rivalry-with-yi-huo",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Tie Ba Xiu’s later roster still lists him among the five rank four peak stage Gu Masters on the mountain.",
      "chapters": [
        359
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rivalry-with-yi-huo",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_tie_ba_xiu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After Tie Mu Bai defeats the rank four peak experts and bans demonic Gu Masters from the three kings inheritance, Long Qing Tian and Kong Ri Tian leave the mountain with dark expressions.",
      "chapters": [
        370
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rivalry-with-yi-huo",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_tie_mu_bai",
        "sys_demonic_path"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Wu Shen Tong’s backstory states that a battle with Long Qing Tian’s jade sky Gu poison ruined Wu Shen Tong’s former physique and left poison that Divine Doctor Sheng Shou could only manage, not remove.",
      "chapters": [
        386
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "jade-sky-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_jade_sky_gu",
        "char_divine_doctor_sheng_shou"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Inside a weakened zone of the blessed land, the land spirit shows Fang Yuan a thin Gu Master in a dark blue robe with a gloomy gaze: Long Qing Tian activating his sole rank five poison Gu, jade sky. The text restates the “dyed the sky jade green” title and says jade sky Gu is his core trump card from immemorial times, now fundamentally extinct, and the basis of his Southern Border poisoning reputation.",
      "chapters": [
        387
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "jade-sky-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_poison_gu",
        "reg_southern_border"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He finds the weakened zone, plans to poison a path to the main world with jade sky Gu, then fights Fang Yuan under the one-Gu restriction of the three kings rules and loses. Narration states Fang Yuan did not kill him: knowing he had no hope of surviving, he smiles darkly, activates jade sky Gu, and kills himself with poison. His corpse is pale jade-green. Fang Yuan cannot safely loot him because the immemorial poison is nearly untreatable outside the four great doctors, and jade sky Gu’s outbreak will hole the land.",
      "chapters": [
        388
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Explorers later find the corpse green-dyed, with the surrounding sky and land dyed a deep green.",
      "chapters": [
        391
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Later explorers find the green-dyed corpse and name him a rank four peak stage famous demonic head who was killed. Driven by greed they run toward the corpse, are infected by the green light, and in less than ten steps turn into green light and dissipate.",
      "chapters": [
        391
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "After rebirth Fang Yuan kills him before he can enter the weakened area, takes his Gu worms, and devours his aperture. Narration contrasts this with the previous life, when jade sky Gu poison blocked loot after the kill.",
      "chapters": [
        400
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_worms"
      ]
    }
  ],
